<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ceará</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ceará is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, on the Atlantic coast, with its capital at Fortaleza. Settled slowly by the Portuguese from the seventeenth century, its dry interior became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> country, and it was long subordinate to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> or Pernambuco. Parts of it joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-equator">Confederation of the Equator</a> in 1824, and in 1884 it became the first Brazilian province to abolish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. Recurrent droughts have driven emigration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ceara.jpg" alt="Ceará" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Srfortes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_do_Cear%C3%A1.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
